{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:420c60d0a682943a","name":"Lightsabers","source":{"id":"source:reference-420c60d0a682943a","title":"Lightsabers","revision":24987,"timestamp":"2024-11-10T16:47:15Z","sha256":"27149753cdda4b00f9f828b79b7f9e83d2417f65f54bc16a5f02fb6c19f3af9a","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=24987","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Lightsabers&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-420c60d0a682943a","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Core Rulebook"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Core_Rulebook"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["This group includes the standard ",{"tag":"a","children":["Lightsaber"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Lightsaber","referenceId":"reference:987a817de9003439"}," (a handgrip hilt that projects a single blade of energy) and all its variants, including the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Double-Bladed Lightsaber"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Double-Bladed_Lightsaber","referenceId":"reference:eedee53b782242fa"}," (as wielded by Darth Maul in ",{"tag":"i","children":["Episode I: the Phantom Menace"]},"). Lightsabers ignore ",{"tag":"a","children":["Damage Reduction"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Damage_Reduction"}," unless noted otherwise. However, a target's ",{"tag":"a","children":["Shield Rating"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Shield_Rating"}," reduces a Lightsaber's damage normally. ",{"tag":"a","children":["Weapon Proficiency (Lightsabers)"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Weapon_Proficiency_(Lightsabers)"}," is a Starting Feat for ",{"tag":"a","children":["Jedi"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Jedi","referenceId":"reference:0b0e48747027a29d"},".\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Jedi Counseling"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Web Enhancements"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Web_Enhancements"}," (",{"tag":"a","children":["Jedi Counseling"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Jedi_Counseling"},")"]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Q:"]}," There are a lot of custom Lightsabers in ",{"tag":"i","children":["Star Wars"]},", but my group can't decide if they all fall under the Lightsabers Weapon Group. For example, would Lumiya's ",{"tag":"a","children":["Lightwhip"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Lightwhip","referenceId":"reference:195da5c178521fb8"}," or the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Lightsaber Tonfa"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Lightsaber_Tonfa"}," used in ",{"tag":"i","children":["The Force Unleashed"]}," video game be considered Lightsabers or ",{"tag":"a","children":["Exotic Weapons"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Exotic_Weapons"},"?\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["A:"]}," Both the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Lightwhip"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Lightwhip","referenceId":"reference:195da5c178521fb8"}," and the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Guard Shoto"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Guard_Shoto","referenceId":"reference:5486e6d2b62d6be9"},", also known as the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Lightsaber Tonfa"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Lightsaber_Tonfa"},", are part of the Lightsabers Weapon Group.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Weapon Groups"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Weapon_Groups","referenceId":"reference:f1e153dd3a9e4b81"}," are pretty broad; for example, \"",{"tag":"a","children":["Simple Weapons"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Simple_Weapons"},"\" includes ",{"tag":"a","children":["Nets"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Nets"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Slings"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Slings"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Clubs"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Clubs"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Knives"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Knives"},", and many others. We usually don't separate a weapon and call it exotic unless it's particularly bizarre or unusual in design. A ",{"tag":"a","children":["Flamethrower"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Flamethrower","referenceId":"reference:3c07f870ddf7e92b"},", for example, operates by shooting flaming liquid. As a result, you have to arc your shots and anticipate the liquid's splash to get the most out of the weapon, and this is very different from the simple point-and-shoot of a blaster or even a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Missile Launcher"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Missile_Launcher","referenceId":"reference:f5c813188b5889e5"},".\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Similarly, a weapon whose design is sufficiently atypical may earn the exotic designation, and this combined with the Weapon Familiarity trait can provide a little local flavor. ",{"tag":"a","children":["Wookiees"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Wookiees"}," can use ",{"tag":"a","children":["Bowcasters"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Bowcasters"}," and ",{"tag":"a","children":["Gungans"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Gungans"}," can use ",{"tag":"a","children":["Atlatls"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Atlatls"}," because they were raised around them, but offworld characters need to put in a little extra training to effectively operate these unfamiliar weapons.\n"]},"\n","\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Core Weapons"]},"\n",{"tag":"table","children":["\n",{"tag":"tbody","children":[{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"th","children":["WEAPON\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["SIZE\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["COST\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["DAMAGE\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["WEIGHT\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["TYPE\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["AVAILABILITY\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Lightsaber"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Lightsaber","referenceId":"reference:987a817